{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0CI5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-universal-homeomorphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c3c595df3e6cab2cc7f11d7bb73285bfa9ca9141459e896b7117cec14919ebaf", "source_text": "Universal homeomorphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bb44577a8a706f8788443e83ab27ffdb93c047f67b5b64a9567864a5d2c4463", "unit_id": "tag:0CI5:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CI5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:644125e35daf6aeb2ae6b3b783438979dbba2e2c0cdd52d35b1631c79f50788a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by\nalgebraic spaces. In\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be a universal homeomorphism.\nHere is another characterization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15c2d99416f1dbcb34a6b3500dd4fe735cd6567facbe9428eb222ebc931a5c70", "unit_id": "tag:0CI5:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CI5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d5aeb9363e6c0460c4d8ca174db9b6e52fab48bca0eb728566dbe3f6bc86cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:823367dcd3ff809672f4d4640d060f55f41f7b35862bdea23e2ea630d7a36f8b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nalgebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is a universal homeomorphism (Properties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>), and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every morphism of algebraic stacks <MATH_0003>\nthe map of topological spaces\n<MATH_0004> is\na homeomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f3cb560d2b4d9311329d9c20b2dfb6300cf6e4b1829e942231cd7bf09c3943b", "unit_id": "tag:0CI6:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CI5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |V|$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|V| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\longrightarrow\n|V| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Z}|} |\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09aa1f8c8ad23cd19dc339d90766602caa1ad31ba2d799a54bf34d02f2619393", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e71c2a3c7e33472248b2bad56aacbc0bf444d45ba211d9863e39419187b9b73e", "source_text": "Assume (1), and let <MATH_0001> be as in (2).\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>.\nBy assumption the morphism <MATH_0004>\nof algebraic spaces is a universal homeomorphism, in particular the map\n<MATH_0005> is a homeomorphism. By\nProperties of Stacks, Section <REF_0001>\nin the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nthe horizontal arrows are open and surjective, and moreover\n<MATH_0007>\nis surjective. Hence as the left vertical arrow is a homeomorphism\nit follows that the right vertical arrow is a homeomorphism. This proves (2).\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0008> (1) follows from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:492c3ecbe37d2089767a7b006990817f78ced6aa4d4a27abde2ac1d0c34e2f30", "unit_id": "tag:0CI6:proof"}
